{:edb/db-before-t 1319 :edb/db-after-t 1320 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534632 50 #inst "2026-10-12T05:21:52.822Z" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186194874 1075 #edb/ref 17592186194875 13194139534632 17592186045417 false] [17592186194874 1075 #edb/ref 17592186194876 13194139534632 17592186045417 false] [17592186194874 1075 #edb/ref 17592186194877 13194139534632 17592186045417 false] [17592186194874 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430188 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186194874 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430194 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186194874 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430200 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186194874 1078 #edb/ref 17592186430188 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186198102 1071 "Write down $\\lnot P(x)$ given that\n![](images/76/76d3525ff67cd5e1d597c4bdbe7b056cefb528405f596fa19a02f7f19bd031ef.png)" 13194139534632 17592186045417 false] [17592186198102 1071 "Write down $\\lnot P(x)$ given that\n![](images/ed/ed810318e9b5d6e76b77735530ff9312af66f936d7c8e197d6dd0fb99227dcb8.svg)" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186198102 1074 "The symbol \"$\\neg$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n![](images/97/976e6fe9a107732c81210776e49cfe3f68939512c0fad63739e2f59acb17f109.svg) \n\nIn other words, $x$ is smaller than $10.$ Therefore, $\\neg P(x)$ means the following:\n![](images/dc/dca132f34f73e2f5987a803e592c1f664cc790ed83ec204205975c401280038c.svg)" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186198102 1074 "The symbol \"$\\neg$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n![](images/c4/c4fcfc8fc10ea5b0cd7ee476d43cee41056e5c398aec7d4b9ca9f10dbc12c5d0.png) \n\nIn other words, $x$ is smaller than $10.$ Therefore, $\\neg P(x)$ means the following:\n![](images/92/92d40318f07563c997405d3f0002d479379bbce2cf8b88d7145e40fac1eb867c.png)" 13194139534632 17592186045417 false] [17592186198457 1038 #edb/ref 17592186430212 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186198457 1038 #edb/ref 17592186430214 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186198458 1038 #edb/ref 17592186430215 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186198458 1038 #edb/ref 17592186430216 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186198459 1038 #edb/ref 17592186430213 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186198515 1050 420.0 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186198708 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186198708 1071 "Find the truth set of $¬P(x)$ given the following predicate defined over the universal set of positive integers between $1$ and $10$, inclusive:\n\n$P(x)$: $x$ is prime" 13194139534632 17592186045417 false] [17592186198708 1071 "Find the truth set of $¬P(x)$ given the following predicate defined over the universal set of positive integers between $1$ and $10,$ inclusive: \n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x$ is prime" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186198708 1074 "The truth set of $¬P(x)$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{¬P}={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P},\n$$\n\nThe truth set of $P(x)$ is the set of primes between $1$ and $10,$ inclusive, i.e.,\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=\\{2,3,5,7\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{¬P} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P} \\\\  & =\\overset{―}{\\{2,3,5,7\\}} \\\\  & =\\{1,4,6,8,9,10\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186199522 1064 "The **negation** of the predicate $P(x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n)$ is a new predicate that we denote as follows:\n\n$$\n\\lnot P(x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n)\n$$\n\nThis predicate is true if and only if $P$ is false for a specific set of assignment variables $x_1,x_2, \\ldots x_n.$\n\nFor example, consider the following predicate defined over the universal set $\\mathbb Z.$\n\n$\\qquad$ *$P(m):$ $m$ is even*\n\nThen, $\\lnot P(m)$ is a new predicate that reads as follows:\n\n$\\qquad$ *$m$ is **not** even*\n\nThis can be simplified as:\n\n$\\qquad$ *$m$ is odd*\n\nFor example:\n\n- $P(2)$ is true while $\\lnot P(2)$ is false\n\n- $P(3)$ is false while $\\lnot P(3)$ is true" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186199522 1064 "The **negation** of the predicate $P(x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n)$ is a new predicate that we denote as follows: $$\\lnot P(x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n)$$ This predicate is true if and only if $P$ is false for a specific set of assignment variables $x_1,x_2, \\ldots x_n.$\n\nFor example, consider the following predicate defined over the universal set $\\mathbb Z.$\n\n$\\qquad$ *$P(m):$ $m$ is even*\n\nThen, $\\lnot P(m)$ is a new predicate that reads as follows:\n\n$\\qquad$ *$m$ is **not** even*\n\nThis can be simplified as:\n\n$\\qquad$ *$m$ is odd*\n\nFor example:\n\n- $P(2)$ is true while $\\lnot P(2)$ is false\n- $P(3)$ is false while $\\lnot P(3)$ is true" 13194139534632 17592186045417 false] [17592186199543 1064 "Let $T_P$ be the truth set of the predicate $P(x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n).$\n\nFrom the definition of the negation of a predicate, we have that $\\lnot P$ is true if and only if $P$ is false. Therefore, the truth set of $\\neg P$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P{:}$\n\n$$\nT_{\\neg P} = \\overline{T}_P\n$$\n\nFor example, consider the following predicate defined over the universal set $\\mathbb{R}{:}$\n\n$P(x):$ $-2x +3 \\leq 5$\n\nTo find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+3 & \\le 5 \\\\ -2x & \\le 2 \\\\ x & \\ge -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is $T_P = [-1,\\infty).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{¬P} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P} \\\\  & =\\overset{―}{[-1,\\infty )} \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186199543 1064 "Let $T_P$ be the truth set of the predicate $P(x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n).$\n\nFrom the definition of the negation of a predicate, we have that $\\lnot P$ is true if and only if $P$ is false. Therefore, the truth set of $\\neg P$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P{:}$\n\n$$T_{\\neg P} = \\overline{T}_P$$\n\nFor example, consider the following predicate defined over the universal set $\\mathbb{R}{:}$\n\n$P(x):$ $-2x +3 \\leq 5$\n\nTo find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}-2x+3 & \\le 5 \\\\ -2x & \\le 2 \\\\ x & \\ge -1\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is $T_P = [-1,\\infty).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}{T}_{¬P} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P} \\\\ & =\\overset{―}{[-1,\\infty )} \\\\ & =(-\\infty ,-1).\\end{aligned}$$" 13194139534632 17592186045417 false] [17592186430179 1080 "x\\le \\pi " 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430179 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430179 1083 #uuid "1265bd5a-78cd-5b77-952d-2c9a8def8f52" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430180 1080 "(-\\infty ,2)" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430180 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430180 1083 #uuid "18f25b9b-3d35-56ca-9327-f8285b1ec334" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430181 1080 "x<y" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430181 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430181 1083 #uuid "24b5f8c2-2b99-5562-891b-303dd931bed9" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430182 1080 "$x$ is not greater than $3$" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430182 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430182 1083 #uuid "24ec13d9-ba04-5cf2-871e-2d3da08d0af9" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430183 1080 "$x$ is smaller than $y$" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430183 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430183 1083 