 smaller than $y.$\n\nThe predicate $P(x,y)$ is given above. Which of following represents $¬P(x,y)?$" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430212 1072 #uuid "0373eae5-d413-558b-aff8-967aba0289ff" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430212 1074 "The symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $x$ is smaller than $y.$\n\nIn other words, $x$ is greater than or equal to $y.$ Therefore, $¬P(x,y)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is greater than or equal to $y.$" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430213 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430208 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430213 1069 "q-175518" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430213 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430213 1071 "Find the truth set of $¬P(x)$ given the following predicate defined over the universal set $R:$\n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x-7<-9$" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430213 1072 #uuid "2f501796-fc0b-5879-8eb1-568ded583cc8" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430213 1074 "The truth set of $¬P(x)$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{¬P}={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\n$$\n\nTo find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-7 & <-9 \\\\ x & <-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is\n${T}_{P}=(-\\infty ,-2).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{¬P} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P} \\\\  & =\\overset{―}{(-\\infty ,-2)} \\\\  & =[-2,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430214 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430211 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430214 1069 "q-175413" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430214 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430214 1071 "$\\,$ $x$ is smaller than or equal to $3.$\n\nThe predicate $P(x)$ is given above. Which of following represents $¬P(x)?$" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430214 1072 #uuid "33e4bfa0-0240-5076-a3cc-c397d31c6632" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430214 1074 "The symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $x$ is smaller than or equal to $3.$\n\nIn other words, $x$ is greater than $3.$ Therefore, $¬P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is greater than $3.$" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430215 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430210 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430215 1069 "q-176028" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430215 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430215 1071 "$\\,$ $x\\ge y$\n\nThe predicate $P(x,y)$ is given above. Which of following represents $¬P(x,y)?$" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430215 1072 #uuid "8f075ba4-7815-572a-b12a-c4691f9f8fab" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430215 1074 "In plain English, our predicate $P(x,y)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is greater than or equal to $y.$\n\nThe symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. To negate our plain English expression, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $x$ is greater than or equal to $y.$\n\nIn other words, $x$ is *smaller than* $y.$ Therefore, $¬P(x,y)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x<y$" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430216 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430207 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430216 1069 "q-175313" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430216 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430216 1071 "$\\,$ $x≱\\pi $\n\nThe predicate $P(x)$ is given above. Which of following represents $¬P(x)?$" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430216 1072 #uuid "f94afce2-6e2a-536a-8567-c4c1dfc21cb5" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true] [17592186430216 1074 "In plain English, our predicate $P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is not greater than or equal to $\\pi .$\n\nThe symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. To negate our plain English expression, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $x$ is not greater than or equal to $\\pi .$\n\nIn other words, $x$ *is* *greater than or equal to* $\\pi .$ Therefore, $¬P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x\\ge \\pi $" 13194139534632 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-1265bd5a-78cd-5b77-952d-2c9a8def8f52" 17592186430179 "answer-18f25b9b-3d35-56ca-9327-f8285b1ec334" 17592186430180 "answer-24b5f8c2-2b99-5562-891b-303dd931bed9" 17592186430181 "answer-24ec13d9-ba04-5cf2-871e-2d3da08d0af9" 17592186430182 "answer-2ade7d61-5826-5d6e-8c44-465826c146fc" 17592186430183 "answer-2e0baf9c-dfdb-50b1-8d2c-f2950159bc02" 17592186430184 "answer-4277be64-1b71-5d62-a369-59d7b2d5d193" 17592186430185 "answer-4c605d05-6b7a-5db3-b1e6-f476658f16d3" 17592186430186 "answer-54737426-e934-5b9e-a7e3-ee8d5c4c5497" 17592186430187 "answer-58d76e8b-1a86-5ffa-acd2-1fa5e4dbcdfa" 17592186430188 "answer-68ae4d49-f3f0-502a-b9d7-38aa0c211660" 17592186430189 "answer-6d8e47ef-6800-5c53-99fc-6fcc124ca2f5" 17592186430190 "answer-a428c3b8-01de-5e8f-b73b-74fada2e9234" 17592186430191 "answer-a48dea4d-1fe6-5b8f-813a-9fa35ad0c35e" 17592186430192 "answer-a6a130d7-695f-5eff-b612-a89637d42af1" 17592186430193 "answer-a8df4836-12c1-578d-98ab-34cb7a048b5a" 17592186430194 "answer-af5653ad-ac62-587a-bac4-a6048e331507" 17592186430195 "answer-b34e3514-08c0-5818-a19c-8df103450dd9" 17592186430196 "answer-ba9859b4-7393-5df1-a3c2-e0b992884a5c" 17592186430197 "answer-bad69646-8267-5dda-8461-557726caa010" 17592186430198 "answer-c186e2f7-ceca-5bf5-